<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to buy May 11-31 N+A naphtha.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to buy May 11-31 N+A naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to buy 28,000 tonnes of napthenic and aromatic (N+A) naphtha for delivery May 11-31, a company offcial said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender seeks offers by March 24 and valid for a day, on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis to Kaohsiung.</p>
<p>CPC's last purchase of N+A in early March for April 16-30 delivery was at $210-$215 per tonne on a c-and-f basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
